  "decision_conditions": [
    "Occupier",
    "The development must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date hereof.\r\rReason: To comply with Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, as amended.",
    "The development must be carried out in accordance with the provisions of the Planning Fire Safety Reasonable Exception Statement prepared by Ashley Cadman dated 23/06/26.\r\rReason: To ensure that the development incorporates the necessary fire safety measures in accordance with the Mayor's London Plan Policy D12.\r",
    "Prior to the operation of the development the applicant shall provide a scheme to the Local Planning Authority for its written approval detailing sound transmission reduction measures to be installed between the ground floor use and the first floor flat. The scheme shall be designed in accordance with the recommendations outlined in the Noise and Vibration Impact Assessment, dated August 2026, prepared by Addiscombe Environmental Consultants Limited (Reference: 1828N) and provide at least Dntw+Ctr 50 DB. Once agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority the approved details shall be installed prior to the development being occupied and retained thereafter.\r\rReason: To protect neighbour amenity in accordance with Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The Launderette hereby permitted shall only operate between the daytime hours of 06:00 and 22:00 Monday - Sunday, as outlined in the Noise and Vibration Impact Assessment dated August 2026, prepared by Addiscombe Environmental Consultants Limited (Reference: 1828N).\r\rReason: To ensure that there is no undue impact on neighbour amenity in accordance with Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018. \r"
  ],
